\ A module's struct getter and user generic, called by qualified name, must dispatch to their
\ methods in a compiled binary. The module binding `m` never reaches the binary, so each word has
\ to be filed under its module and bare name, the way a `use` import of it would be.

m: "fixtures/qualified_module_generic_mod.1z" load ;

3 4 m.make-point m.x>> .
5 m.kind print-line
"hi" m.kind print-line
